{"event_type":"review","id":"aa047866891ea7069bbc70bcbb26f864dd30f70735cb6369bf090b75b3a26952","occurred_at":"2026-11-14T21:35:16Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c82c92acab995789cf46e17b19bb3395d5693741e4d6ba29d169f77264e4d849","sha256":"c82c92acab995789cf46e17b19bb3395d5693741e4d6ba29d169f77264e4d849"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3c26506f5ffad5ba34c0cc5ff483c0f76b1de36ce785fb7cbb424a8ffcb972bb","sha256":"3c26506f5ffad5ba34c0cc5ff483c0f76b1de36ce785fb7cbb424a8ffcb972bb"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a424a7bcd8eb914dd733aca2f24fcd5551c2375ee7d4cb503029fe7ecb54162e","sha256":"a424a7bcd8eb914dd733aca2f24fcd5551c2375ee7d4cb503029fe7ecb54162e"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/60a64fdeb64f9a65f8caf616314656300ca9b332f93bb7bf00be6d7eac480741","sha256":"60a64fdeb64f9a65f8caf616314656300ca9b332f93bb7bf00be6d7eac480741"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0d42b583c5086b71a378caa8c9a1aceb5259900454a0c752af7b54ffc92636e7","sha256":"0d42b583c5086b71a378caa8c9a1aceb5259900454a0c752af7b54ffc92636e7"}],"attempt_id":"430e5b3e0273beaab4cc4a59b186def060bcc92a7f222ec665bca5279a06805a:0:1","base":"9e0d5aeec9c7c7a43e80f76595261e1f24f7580b","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"84fe342be051ec2a7d329615b85a563e92392c4c","body":"**Use a path-component check to exclude checkout executables.**\n\nFor a checkout at `/repo`, `/repo/..tools/git` produces the relative path `..tools/git`. This condition accepts that path because it starts with `..`. `terminalGit()` then executes the in-checkout file as the trusted Git executable.\n\nRequire an actual parent component (`..` or `..` followed by the platform separator), rather than a string prefix.","id":"4a213876de6a247cac1539ce0b1368ab631d297560c38253af61577b60f2a760","intervals":[[237,237]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressEvidence.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Use a path-component check to exclude checkout executables."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"84fe342be051ec2a7d329615b85a563e92392c4c","body":"**Clear the cached terminal session after disposal.**\n\nWhen a stale checkout is refreshed after a terminal session exists, the next terminal Git operation can fail. `disposeAddressTerminalSession` removes the session directory but keeps `terminalSessions[token]`. The `removed` hook then sets the owner active again on the next `activateCheckout`. `terminalSession` returns the cached session, whose directory no longer exists.\n\nDelete the cache entry after the directory removal succeeds. Early returns keep the entry, so a replaced environment still fails closed.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n   await rmdir(session.directory);\n+  terminalSessions.delete(token);\n }\n```\n\n</details>","id":"fa10a48665e40c2b1459d56ebff29b6503a73d8350f47469387e6de0c8683d03","intervals":[[597,597]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressEvidence.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Clear the cached terminal session after disposal."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"bad378d6a85c192b05677f6d47eab88f101b43e9","body":"**Settle cancelled attempts of participants closed without arrival.**\n\nA participant whose `action()` rejects skips `arrive()` and is closed in `finally`. `runTerminal()` then builds the cancelled-attempt list only from open participants, so a receipt deferred before that rejection never reaches `settleAddressTerminalEvidence()`. If the attempt's action rejects after `restore()` defers the receipt, that cancelled evidence stays unsettled.\n\nCollect cancelled attempts from every participant. Release never removes a cancelled attempt, so the closed participant still holds it.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-      const attempts = open.flatMap((entry) =>\n+      const attempts = [...this.participants].flatMap((entry) =>\n         entry.attempts.filter((attempt) => attempt.cancelled),\n       );\n```\n\n</details>","id":"7c3a57f82901f41275ec5e86a6f59c20899cad342c5d6defaa3caf6eeb3393ac","intervals":[[282,283]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressRunLifecycle.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Settle cancelled attempts of participants closed without arrival."}],"head":"910aaedebf4656cdcf1976abaf03257d12f6f900","head_tree":"1ecd116c4ac33bbae984033dfd03894947e6454f","input_scope":[{"blob":"93aac939c418cac6062b8e8f3dc9b2566d391016","intervals":[[1,497]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressCheckoutOwnership.ts"},{"blob":"84fe342be051ec2a7d329615b85a563e92392c4c","intervals":[[1,1018]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressEvidence.ts"},{"blob":"bad378d6a85c192b05677f6d47eab88f101b43e9","intervals":[[1,633]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressRunLifecycle.ts"},{"blob":"ba1165856848c14d07f127841131234011458d1a","intervals":[[1,66]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/areaReviewPlan.ts"},{"blob":"d38e6866cca8c97f10aa71da93cd2e92678836c8","intervals":[[1,80]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/localReview.ts"}],"job_id":"430e5b3e0273beaab4cc4a59b186def060bcc92a7f222ec665bca5279a06805a:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"93aac939c418cac6062b8e8f3dc9b2566d391016","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressCheckoutOwnership.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"84fe342be051ec2a7d329615b85a563e92392c4c","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressEvidence.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"bad378d6a85c1